# Normalise line endings in the repository, whatever the checkout host does. The work happens on a
# WSL host, in two Linux containers and on whatever CI runs, and a CRLF that reaches a committed
# shell script makes it fail with an unreadable `\r: not found`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by controller-gen, and committed on purpose: DeepCopyObject() is what satisfies
# runtime.Object, so without this file api/v1alpha1 does not compile -- a fresh clone could not
# build or vet until someone had run `make generate`, which first downloads controller-gen.
#
# linguist-generated collapses it in review and keeps it out of the language statistics. It is not
# `-diff`: a deepcopy change nobody expected means an API type changed shape, which is worth
# seeing when asked for.
api/**/zz_generated.*.go linguist-generated=true
